---
import DrawbridgeLayout from "@/layouts/DrawbridgeLayout.astro";
---

<DrawbridgeLayout
  title="Rubric → Canvas CSV reference"
  description="Detailed reference for the Rubric → Canvas CSV tool."
>
  <article class="grid gap-8">
    <div class="grid gap-2">
      <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl">Rubric → Canvas CSV: Reference</h1>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground">Input formats, points presets, edge cases, and CSV output details.</p>
    </div>

    <section class="grid gap-3">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">Expected table shape</h2>
      <p>
        The source table should have one row per criterion and one column per rating level. The first two columns are
        reserved:
      </p>
      <ol class="list-decimal space-y-1 pl-5">
        <li><strong>Criterion name</strong></li>
        <li><strong>Points</strong> — the maximum points for that criterion</li>
        <li><strong>Rating columns</strong> — one column per rating level, left to right from highest to lowest</li>
      </ol>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border">
        <table class="w-full text-sm">
          <thead class="bg-muted/50">
            <tr>
              <th class="px-4 py-2 text-left font-medium">Criterion</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-2 text-left font-medium">Points</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-2 text-left font-medium">Exemplary</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-2 text-left font-medium">Proficient</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-2 text-left font-medium">Developing</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr class="border-t">
              <td class="px-4 py-2">Organization</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2">4</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2">Clear and logical</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2">Mostly logical</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2">Unclear</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="grid gap-3">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">Supported import formats</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
        <li><strong>Word .docx</strong> — tables extracted directly from the document.</li>
        <li><strong>Rich paste from Word</strong> — copy a table and paste it as HTML.</li>
        <li><strong>Markdown pipe table</strong> — plain text with <code>|</code> delimiters.</li>
        <li><strong>Tab-separated text</strong> — copied from a spreadsheet.</li>
        <li><strong>Canvas rubric CSV</strong> — a CSV previously exported from this tool or from Canvas.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="grid gap-3">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">Points presets</h2>
      <dl class="grid gap-2 text-sm">
        <div class="grid gap-1 sm:grid-cols-[1fr_2fr]">
          <dt class="font-medium">Full / Half / Zero / Zero</dt>
          <dd>First rating = full points, second = half (rounded), remaining ratings = 0.</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="grid gap-1 sm:grid-cols-[1fr_2fr]">
          <dt class="font-medium">Evenly spaced</dt>
          <dd>Points decrease evenly from full points down to 0.</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="grid gap-1 sm:grid-cols-[1fr_2fr]">
          <dt class="font-medium">Custom percentages</dt>
          <dd>Enter a percentage of the criterion points for each rating level.</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="grid gap-1 sm:grid-cols-[1fr_2fr]">
          <dt class="font-medium">Manual</dt>
          <dd>Every rating point is set by hand; presets do not change it.</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </section>

    <section class="grid gap-3">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">Output CSV format</h2>
      <p>
        The exported CSV follows the Canvas rubric import format: one row per criterion, with ratings flattened into
        repeating <code>Rating Name, Rating Description, Rating Points</code> triplets. Rows may be ragged when
        criteria have different numbers of ratings.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="grid gap-3">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">Edge cases</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
        <li>
          <strong>Missing rating cells</strong> — empty cells in a rating column are treated as skipped rating levels.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Different criteria, different counts</strong> — some criteria may have fewer ratings than others. The
          tool preserves this when exporting.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Manual overrides</strong> — points edited by hand are highlighted and kept when presets change until
          you reset them.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </article>
</DrawbridgeLayout>
